// Windows resource file: builds retroapl.ico into retroapl.exe, so the
// program shows its icon in Explorer, on shortcuts and on the taskbar.
// IDI_ICON1 is the name Qt looks for as the default icon for its windows.
// Compiled only on Windows (see CMakeLists.txt). Linux builds the same
// .ico in through retroapl.qrc instead.

IDI_ICON1 ICON "retroapl.ico"
